  "Question": "Which of the following statements about relative frequency and probability is correct?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Over a large number of repeated trials, the relative frequency of an event stabilizes near its probability.",
    "B": "Relative frequency always equals probability.",
    "C": "With only 10 trials, the relative frequency must equal the probability.",
    "D": "Probability changes as the number of trials increases."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Probability is a fixed number, while relative frequency fluctuates during trials. Only when the number of trials is very large does the relative frequency stabilize near the probability.",
